# MSI/MSI-X for PCI devices.
#
# Without this every virtio queue interrupt falls back to legacy INTx: a
# shared, level-triggered line the VMM must assert and the guest must
# acknowledge. MSI-X gives each queue its own edge-triggered vector.
#
# Against the virtio-fs check set, boot to init is unchanged (~42ms vs
# ~44ms with printk quiet, inside the noise) and I/O time is unchanged
# to 3ms. The whole check set raises only ~172 interrupts, so per-queue
# vectors have nothing to save.
#
# Enable it for a guest that drives virtio-net or multiqueue virtio-blk,
# where interrupt rates are orders of magnitude higher and INTx shares
# one line across every queue. Measure that workload. This one cannot
# show the difference.
CONFIG_PCI_MSI=y
